{
  "openapi" : "3.1.0",
  "info" : {
    "title" : "Spring Security JWT Audit API",
    "description" : "REST API secured with JWT: a short-lived access token in the `Authorization` header and a long-lived refresh token in an `HttpOnly` cookie, rotated on every use.\n\n**Authenticating in this page**\n1. Call `POST /api/v1/auth/login` with one of the demo accounts (`admin` / `manager` / `user`, password `Demo1234!`).\n2. Copy `authToken` from the response.\n3. Click **Authorize** and paste it. The token is valid for 15 minutes.\n\nThe refresh cookie is set by the browser and scoped to `/api/v1/auth`, so `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh` works from this page without pasting anything.\n\n**Roles** are hierarchical: `SYSTEM` > `ADMIN` > `MANAGER` > `USER`. A role inherits every permission below it.\n\nAuthentication endpoints are rate limited per client IP and answer `429` with a `Retry-After` header once the limit is hit.",
    "contact" : {
      "name" : "PaulStna",
      "url" : "https://github.com/PaulStna"
    },
    "license" : {
      "name" : "MIT",
      "url" : "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"
    },
    "version" : "v1"
  },
  "servers" : [ {
    "url" : "/",
    "description" : "This server"
  } ],
  "tags" : [ {
    "name" : "Authentication",
    "description" : "Obtaining, rotating and revoking tokens. The access token is returned in the body; the refresh token is set as an HttpOnly cookie scoped to /api/v1/auth and is rotated on every refresh."
  }, {
    "name" : "Users",
    "description" : "User administration. Every operation needs an access token, and the required role is stated per operation. Roles are hierarchical, so ADMIN satisfies anything MANAGER can do."
  } ],
